S1: Services per Membership app, by type

fetch dt.entity.service
| fields id, serviceType, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| summarize apmids = collectDistinct(splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]), by:{id, serviceType}
| filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
| fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0]
| filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| summarize services = count(), apps = countDistinctExact(apmid), by:{serviceType}
| sort services desc


This shows how many are web request services and how many are database or background services. Only web request and web services feed the failure-rate and slow-service tiles.

S2: JVM coverage on Membership processes

timeseries gc = avg(dt.runtime.jvm.gc.suspension_time, scalar: true),
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}, from:-2h
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
    | fields id, tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
    | summarize apmids = collectDistinct(splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]), by:{id}
    | filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
    | fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0]
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "p."
| filter in(p.apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| summarize jvms = count(), apps = countDistinctExact(p.apmid),
            avgGc = round(avg(gc), decimals:2), maxGc = round(max(gc), decimals:2)


If apps is very low, I'd drop the JVM tile. If it's high, maxGc helps set a threshold.

S3: Process-level coverage and size

timeseries {mem = avg(dt.process.memory.working_set_size),
            cpu = avg(dt.process.cpu.usage)},
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}, from:-2h
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
    | fields id, tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
    | summarize apmids = collectDistinct(splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]), by:{id}
    | filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
    | fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0]
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "p."
| filter in(p.apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| summarize processes = count(),
            maxMemGiB = round(max(arrayAvg(mem)) / 1073741824, decimals:2),
            maxCpuPct = round(max(arrayAvg(cpu)), decimals:1),
            by:{apmid = p.apmid}
| sort maxMemGiB desc
